    description: "WHAT. PR #2198 fixed the non-id edge endpoints of 15 analyzers. A throwaway AST sweep over Edge(src=/dst=) expressions found more, none verified by fixture: linkers/pyffi.py:413, linkers/ruby_ffi.py:274, fortran.py:881,920, hlsl.py:272, latex.py:286,299,326,339,350,378, matlab.py:283, meson.py:358, nix.py:499,500,529, puppet.py:434, purescript.py:549, r_lang.py:488,490, racket.py:434, robot.py:472,473,547, scheme.py:365, gleam.py:290,291, odin.py:306,307, prisma.py:311, twig.py:178,233,284, v_lang.py:516,517, verilog.py (the external module dst), vhdl.py:319, powershell.py:223,253, xml_config.py:251 (line numbers as of dev 2e41d7d686). The sweep cannot see an endpoint passed through a parameter, so the list is a lower bound.\n\nASK. Verify each with a fixture, fix with analyze/edge_target.py's helpers, and extend scripts/check-id-construction to edge endpoints so the next one is caught statically. The verilog/vhdl external module id (verilog:external:<type>:module) is hashed into the stand-in's stable id: fixing its shape changes stand-in ids. Found during PR 1 of the stable-id plan, 2026-11-15 (PR #2198). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr1/STATUS.md."  # 72df
